      "text": "$$\\begin{align*}\n(2x - 5)(x + 7) - (x + 5)(2x - 1) &= 2x^2 + 14x - 5x - 35 - (2x^2 - x + 10x - 5) \\\\\n&= 2x^2 + 9x - 35 - 2x^2 + x - 5 \\\\\n&= 10x - 40 \\\\\n&= \\boxed{10(x - 4)}\n\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe problem is about simplifying a polynomial expression. The first step is to expand the two binomials, $(2x - 5)(x + 7)$ and $(x + 5)(2x - 1)$. For the first binomial, we distribute each term in $(2x - 5)$ across $(x + 7)$, resulting in $2x^2 + 14x - 5x - 35$. For the second binomial, we distribute each term in $(x + 5)(2x - 1)$ across $(x + 7)$, resulting in $2x^2 - x + 10x - 5$. \n\nNext, we combine like terms. Combining the like terms for the first binomial simplifies it to $2x^2 + 9x - 35$. Similarly, combining the like terms for the second binomial simplifies it to $2x^2 + 9x - 5$. \n\nFinally, we subtract the two simplified binomials, $2x^2 + 9x - 35$ and $2x^2 + 9x - 5$, resulting in $10x - 40$. \n\nTherefore, the simplified expression is $10x - 40$. In conclusion, $(2x - 5)(x + 7) - (x + 5)(2x - 1)$ simplifies to $\\boxed{10(x - 4)}$.",
