      "text": "To solve the expression \\((2x - 5)(x + 7) - (x + 5)(2x - 1)\\), we will first expand each binomial product and then combine like terms. Here is the step-by-step process:\n\n1. Expand \\((2x - 5)(x + 7)\\):\n\\[\n(2x - 5)(x + 7) = 2x \\cdot x + 2x \\cdot 7 - 5 \\cdot x - 5 \\cdot 7 = 2x^2 + 14x - 5x - 35 = 2x^2 + 9x - 35\n\\]\n\n2. Expand \\((x + 5)(2x - 1)\\):\n\\[\n(x + 5)(2x - 1) = x \\cdot 2x + x \\cdot (-1) + 5 \\cdot 2x + 5 \\cdot (-1) = 2x^2 - x + 10x - 5 = 2x^2 + 9x - 5\n\\]\n\n3. Substitute the expanded forms back into the original expression:\n\\[\n(2x^2 + 9x - 35) - (2x^2 + 9x - 5)\n\\]\n\n4. Combine like terms:\n\\[\n2x^2 + 9x - 35 - 2x^2 - 9x + 5 = (2x^2 - 2x^2) + (9x - 9x) + (-35 + 5) = 0 + 0 - 30 = -30\n\\]\n\nThe simplified expression is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-30}\n\\]",
