      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "\\begin{align*}\n&(2x - 5)(x + 7) - (x + 5)(2x - 1) \\\\\n&= 2x^{2} + 14x - 5x - 35 - (2x^{2} - x + 10x - 5) \\\\\n&= 2x^{2} + 9x - 35 - 2x^{2} + x - 10x + 5 \\\\\n&= \\boxed{x - 30}.\n\\end{align*} To solve the given expression \\((2x - 5)(x + 7) - (x + 5)(2x - 1)\\), we will first expand each part of the expression and then combine like terms.\n\nLet's start with the first part \\((2x - 5)(x + 7)\\):\n\n\\[\n(2x - 5)(x + 7) = 2x \\cdot x + 2x \\cdot 7 - 5 \\cdot x - 5 \\cdot 7 = 2x^2 + 14x - 5x - 35 = 2x^2 + 9x - 35\n\\]\n\nNow, let's expand the second part \\((x + 5)(2x - 1)\\):\n\n\\[\n(x + 5)(2x - 1) = x \\cdot 2x + x \\cdot (-1) + 5 \\cdot 2x + 5 \\cdot (-1) = 2x^2 - x + 10x - 5 = 2x^2 + 9x - 5\n\\]\n\nNext, we substitute these expanded forms back into the original expression:\n\n\\[\n(2x - 5)(x + 7) - (x + 5)(2x - 1) = (2x^2 + 9x - 35) - (2x^2 + 9x - 5)\n\\]\n\nNow, we distribute the negative sign through the second set of parentheses:\n\n\\[\n2x^2 + 9x - 35 - 2x^2 - 9x + 5\n\\]\n\nCombine like terms:\n\n\\[\n(2x^2 - 2x^2) + (9x - 9x) + (-35 + 5) = 0 + 0 - 30 = -30\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the simplified form of the expression is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-30}\n\\]",
